  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Throughout my experience in VRChat, when in a populated world it can become very difficult to listen to those close to you, even if others are further away. To hear people nearby better, I've thought of two potential features.\n\n1. The user(s) within the centre of your screen will remain at their normal volume whilst other voices automatically become more quiet. This could be adjusted to encompass the users' entire cone of vision or just a small portion in the centre. The range of how far in front of you this reaches could also be adjusted.\n\nAND/OR:\n\n2. The option to have an adjustable radius, where everyone outside of the area has their volume lowered. How much the volume is reduced outside of this radius could also be adjusted.\n\nThanks for reading, any and all feedback is welcome.",
